		<SimpleData name="rowlett">2012. Active; focal plane 77 m (253 ft); three white flashes every 20 s. 60 m (197 ft) round concrete tower with lantern and double gallery. Entire lighthouse is white. A 2023 photo is at right and Google has a satellite view. This light is mounted on a vessel traffic control tower. Located at Bhadreswar, a village about 30 km (19 mi) northwest of Mundra. Site open, tower closed. Admiralty F0365; NGA 28378.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/Bhadreshwar%20Vts%20Repeater%20And%20Lighthouse%20Station.png</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(5:Longitude printed without hemisphere letter ('69.9135°'); taken as E,Tower height 60M exceeds stated light elevation 48M above MSL,Items xi-xiii values appear shifted one row: 'Product Life Expectancy: 12/03/2022', 'Date of Installation: Sealite, Australia', Make blank,Vertical divergence given as '&gt;1.5°' (lower bound only),Optic line also states '13 – 19NM AT@ 0.74')</SimpleData>
