		<SimpleData name="rowlett">Date unknown (station established 1892). Active; focal plane about 65 m (213 ft); two white flashes every 15 s. 60 m (197 ft) round cylindrical concrete vessel traffic control tower with lantern and gallery, painted with horizontal black and white bands; lantern roof painted red. Daksh Joshi's 2020 photo is at right, a 2018 photo is available and Google has a satellite view. Navinal Point is a swampy point of land sheltering Mundra Creek; Admiralty F0361.82.</SimpleData>
