		<SimpleData name="ledger_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-12/Master%20Ledger%20Gandhidham%2016.pdf</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-vts-gandhi-dham/mungra-reef-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1890 (rebuilt and lit in 1997; rebuilt a second time in 1999). Active; focal plane 10 m (33 ft); two white flashes every 10 s. 10 m (33 ft) round cylindrical concrete tower on a circular masonry pier. Tower painted red with one white horizontal band. The Indian Logistics Info photo is at right, but the light is not seen in Bing's satellite view. The lighthouse marks a dangerous reef on the approach to Jodiya Bandar. The native state of Nawanagar built this beacon. It was rebuilt in 1999 after being heavily damaged by a tropical cyclone on 9 June 1998. Located in the Gulf of Kachchh about 12 km (7.5 mi) northwest of Jodiya Bandar. Accessible only by boat. Site and tower closed. ARLHS IND-151;</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-151</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/Mungra_Reef_Lighthouse.png</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
