		<SimpleData name="ledger_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-12/Master%20Ledger%20Gandhidham%2013.pdf</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-vts-gandhi-dham/jodiya-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">2002 (station established 1903). Active; focal plane 31 m (102 ft); white flash every 10 s. 30 m (98 ft) skeletal tower, painted white. A 2021 photo and a distant 2025 view are available and Google has a satellite view. The 1993 lighthouse, a round cylindrical masonry tower with gallery attached to a small square 1-story equipment room, was destroyed by the earthquake of 26 January 2001. The original lighthouse was a small cast iron tower purchased from Chance Brothers by the native state of Nawanagar. Located at Jodiya (Jodia), a small port on the upper Gulf of Kachchh. Site open, tower closed. ARLHS IND-141; Admiralty F0368; NGA 28368.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-141</SimpleData>
