		<SimpleData name="ledger_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-12/Master%20Ledger%20Gandhidham%2018_0.pdf</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-vts-gandhidham/mawadi-point-beacon</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1958 (station established 1928). Active; focal plane 8 m (26 ft); red flash every 10 s. 8 m (26 ft) short round tower mounted atop a round cylindrical stone tower. The upper tower is painted red with a white horizontal band. The lower tower is unpainted brown stone. Tushar Chhatrara has a photo but the light is not shown in Google's satellite view. The light marks the end of a reef extending northeast from Pirotan Island. The first light was a skeletal tower built on a daybecaon established in 1867. Located about 2.25 km (1.4 mi) northeast of the modern lighthouse. Site open, and nothing prevents climbing on the lighthouse. Admiralty F0378; NGA 28356.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q29048448</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Lighthouse%20pirotan.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(1:Elevation 5 Meter is less than tower height 8 Meter)</SimpleData>
