		<SimpleData name="ledger_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-12/Master%20Ledger%20Gandhidham%2019.pdf</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-vts-gandhidham/bural-reef-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1979. Active; focal plane 15 m (49 ft); quick-flashing white light. 12 m (39 ft) round cylindrical concrete tower with three galleries but no lantern, painted white. Lightphotos.net has an older photo, Indian Logistics Info.has a page with a photo, and Bing has a satellite view. The dangerous Bural Reef extends east northeast from Okha Point. Located about 25 km (15 mi) east northeast of Okha. Accessible only by boat. Site and tower closed. ARLHS IND-126; Admiralty F0386.5; NGA 28328.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-126</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/Bural_Reef_Lighthouse%20.png</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:Station name not printed in ledger; taken from file slug,Luminous range 9NM conflicts with lantern electrical parameter range 11-14NM,Year of commissioning 1978, with new light &amp; trestle 05.02.2022)</SimpleData>
