		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-vts-gandhi-dham/samiyani-north-island-lighthouse-station</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">2002 (station established 1935). Active; focal plane 11 m (36 ft); green flash every 3 s. 9 m (30 ft) round cylindrical concrete tower, mounted on a concrete foundation. Lighthouse painted with black and white horizontal bands. Chetan Kanzariya has a distant view and Google has an indistinct satellite view. The original light on a skeletal tower was replaced by a concrete tower in 1957. That lighthouse was destroyed by a tropical cyclone on 9 June 1998. It was replaced by a temporary skeletal tower, and then by the present lighthouse, which probably resembles the 1957 tower. Located in the water off the northeast tip of Samiyani Island. , marking the end of a long shoal. Accessible only by b</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-163</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/Samiyani_North_Island_Lighthouse_Station.png</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(1:Latitude printed as '22°29 5&quot;N' without a minutes mark; read as 22° 29' 5&quot;)</SimpleData>
