		<SimpleData name="ledger_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-12/Master%20Ledger%20Gandhidham%2025.pdf</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-vts-gandhi-dham/samiyani-island-lighthouse-station</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1876. Active; focal plane 22 m (72 ft); flash every 5 s, white or red depending on direction. 20 m (66 ft) round sandstone tower with lantern and gallery, mounted on a square stone base. Lighthouse painted white; lantern dome is red. A 2018 photo is at right, Kashyap Atri has a 2019 photo, Vishal Ahir has a 2024 view from the sea, and Google has a satellite view. Built by the princely state of Baroda, this elegant and historic lighthouse marks the entrance to Okha harbor. It stands on an island 1.5 km (1 mi) north of Okha Point, the tip of the peninsula. Boat transportation to the island can be hired in Okha. Located in the center of the island. Site open, tower closed. ARLHS IND-018; Admira</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-018</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/Samiyani_island_Lighthouse_Station.png</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(4:No station name printed; address is 'C/o Station in-Charge, Okha Lighthouse and VTS Station',Latitude printed '22°29 3&quot;N' with missing minute mark; read as 22° 29' 3&quot;,Characteristic says white flashing only but visibility sectors include red sectors,Date of commissioning: original 1876, present lighthouse 1927)</SimpleData>
