		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-vts-gandhi-dham/okha-lighthouse-dgps-and-vts-station</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1956. Active; focal plane 26 m (85 ft); three white flashes every 25 s. 23 m (75 ft) square cylindrical concrete tower with lantern and gallery, painted with horizontal red and white bands. Niraj Kumar has a photo. Google's satellite view shows the 60 m (197 ft) round VTS vessel tracking tower built next to the historic lighthouse in 2012. Wikimedia has a view taken from the VTS tower. Okha lies at the end of a north-pointing peninsula that defines the southern entrance to the Gulf of Kachchh (Kutch). After independence western India lost the use of the port of Karachi, Pakistan, so it became important to develop port facilities in the Gulf. This lighthouse was the first major improvement to</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-014</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/OKHA_LIGHTHOUSE.png</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(5:Position printed with seconds using a single prime (34.87', 11.38'); treated as degrees-minutes-seconds,Emergency vertical divergence printed as 0° 68' (minutes &gt;= 60),Optic 'Duration: 5 sec.' conflicts with flash duration 0.41 s in characteristic,RACON and DGPS aerial label/value rows are misaligned on the page (e.g. Output pulse power / Code / Power supply values shifted),DGPS Date Commissioning listed as 30-10-1998 and also 'Date of Commissioning 22/03/2018' / May 2004 in misaligned rows)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ &quot;dgps&quot;: 2018, &quot;racon&quot;: 2004 }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_since">{ &quot;racon&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2004, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;ledger&quot; }, &quot;dgps&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2018, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;ledger&quot; } }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="tenders">(2:2303,622)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo_credit">DGLL</SimpleData>
	</SchemaData></ExtendedData>
