		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1968 (station established 1943). Active; focal plane 30 m (98 ft); two long (1.4 s) white flashes every 20 s. 26 m (85 ft) round cylindrical concrete tower with lantern and gallery, painted with horizontal black and white bands. Sayan Pradhan's 2023 photo is at the top of this page, Wikimdia has Biswarup Ganguly's 2016 photo and several other photos, a 2012 photo is available, and Google has a 2023 street view and a satellite view. The original light was on a 20 m (66 ft) steel mast located 1 km (0.6 mi) to the east. The original optics for the current lighthouse were transferred from the 1881 Dwarka lighthouse, deactivated in 1964. Modern LED optics are now in use. Since 1995 the lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-030</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q32859730</SimpleData>
