		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-jamnagar/perigee-light-vesselmain-light</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1973 (station established 1936). Active; focal plane 12 m (39 ft); white flash every 7 s. 21 m (69 ft) unstaffed steel lightfloat; the solar-powered light is shown from a square pyramidal steel skeletal tower with gallery. Entire vessel painted red. A DGLL photo is at right and Bing has a satellite view. This vessel, the third to serve on the station, marks a dangerous shoal in the channel on the approach to Bhavnagar. Operated as an automated lightfloat, the ship was reported still on station in 2010. Located 3 km (2 mi) northeast of the Ghogha lighthouse; there should be a distant view from the Ghogha waterfront. Site and vessel closed. Operator: DGLL. ARLHS IND-144; Admiralty F0449; NGA 2</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-144</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/J-20.jpg</SimpleData>
