		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-jamnagar/ghogha-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">Date unknown (station established 1856). Active; focal plane 18 m (59 ft); red light occulting once every 15 s. 16 m (52 ft) square (or rectangular) cylindrical masonry tower with lantern and gallery, painted with horizontal red and white bands. Abutalib Sheikh has a closeup 2023 video, Ibrahim Shekh has a 2018 photo, Jatin Shah has a sunrise photo, another photo (second photo on the page) is available, and Google has a fuzzy satellite view. The station was inaugurated in 1856 with a mast light; this was replaced by a cast iron tower in 1887 and then by a masonry tower in 1936. Another tower was built in 1961. (We need more information about the history of this station!) Although Ghogha is a</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-134</SimpleData>
