		<SimpleData name="record">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-12/mm1.pdf</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-mumbai/luhara-point-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1977 (station established 1887). Active; focal plane 32 m (105 ft); white flash every 15 s. 24 m (79 ft) round cast iron tower with lantern and gallery, mounted on a round concrete base. Lighthouse painted in a red and white spiral pattern; lantern painted white. A 2021 photo is at right, Farmesh Vasava has a 2018 photo, Asim Patel has a sunset photo, Prakash Patel has a view from atop the lighthouse, and Google has a satellite view. The original lighthouse was a skeletal tower. Located on a point of land near Ambetha, at the entrance to the Narbada River, which leads to the port city of Bharuch. Accessible by a walk of about 1.5 km (1 mi) from the village of Luhara (local guidance needed). </SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/Luhara_Point_Lighthouse.png</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(2:No. of lens printed 'Acrylic Fresnel lens assembly &amp; 4 lanes +4 Blanks' (octagonal assembly); 4 lenses used,RACON Sr. No 6295 is the same serial as in East Island and Kalpeni ledgers)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ &quot;racon&quot;: 2005 }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_since">{ &quot;racon&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2005, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;ledger&quot; }, &quot;ais&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2012, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;network&quot; } }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="tenders">(2:2544,2219)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo_credit">DGLL</SimpleData>
