		<SimpleData name="tower_type">Round concrete Tower</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="tower_h_m">41</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="tower_colour">Black and White bands</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="tower_year">1983</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="established">1876</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="visit">grounds</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="tourism">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="museum">0</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="record">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-12/dj4.pdf</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-jamnagar/porbandar-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1983 (station established 1876). Active; focal plane 47 m (145 ft); white flash every 5 s. 41 m (135 ft) round concrete tower with lantern and gallery; the lighthouse also has a large harbor control room encircling the tower about 1/3 of the way up from the ground. Lighthouse painted with horizontal black and white bands. Google's 2023 street view is at right, Jayrajsinh Vaghela has a 2022 photo, Bandari Laxman has a 2023 photo, Vijay Jethva has a sunset photo, and Google also has a satellite view. Porbandar is an important port and also a tourist attraction; it was the birthplace of Mahatma Gandhi. Located 4 km (2.5 mi) east of the harbor of Porbandar. Site open, tower reported open in the </SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-158</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/j-4.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:Optic 'Duration of Flash 5 Sec' conflicts with flash 0.25 s in characteristic,Effective beam intensity blank,RACON and NAIS tables blank, yet a 70 W 'Solar Plant for RACON' is listed)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ &quot;ais&quot;: 2018 }</SimpleData>
