		<SimpleData name="record">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-12/dj19.pdf</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-jamnagar/piram-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1865 (extensively rebuilt in 1965). Active; focal plane 42 m (138 ft); two white flashes every 10 s. 27 m (89 ft) round cylindrical masonry tower with lantern and gallery, rising from a circular 2-story base. Lighthouse painted with horizontal black and white bands. V.T. Balar has a 2018 closeup photo and Google has a satellite view. The lighthouse was repaired after a damaging fire in 1928. In 1965 its height was increased by 3 m (10 ft) and a new lantern was installed; photos suggest that only the 2-story base remains from the British lighthouse. The island is privately owned and available for purchase or development. Located on the southwest side of the island, about 10 km (6 mi) southeas</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-006</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/J-18.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(2:NAIS section empty but a 6KWp 'Solar Plant for Main NAIS' and PSS NAIS batteries are listed,Unusually wide divergence 20°59.99' horizontal, 13°44.72' vertical)</SimpleData>
