		<SimpleData name="ledger_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-12/dj5.pdf</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-jamnagar/navibandar-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">Around 1920 (station established 1896). Active; focal plane 18 m (59 ft); white flash every 10 s. 15 m (49 ft) round concrete tower with lantern and gallery. Lighthouse painted white, lantern painted black with a red roof. A closeup photo (nearly 2/3 the way down the page) is available, Virendra Chamundiya has a 2024 closeup, and Google has a 2023 street view and a satellite view. The original light was on a corner of an 18th century fort, otherwise in ruins, that was restored for use as a lighthouse. This light is easily confused with the Nawabandar Light just east of Diu; that lighthouse is listed and pictured above. The two lighthouses are twins, which increases the chance of confusion. L</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-153</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/J-5.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(2:Optic Duration of Flash printed as '10 Sec', inconsistent with characteristic 1+9=10 Sec,Effective beam intensity fields are blank)</SimpleData>
