		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1965. Active; focal plane 36 m (118 ft); white flash every 3 s. 24 m (79 ft) hexagonal cylindrical masonry tower with lantern and gallery, painted with horizontal black and white bands. Allott Christian has a 2019 photo, Shreyesh Abhavani has a 2023 photo, and Google has a satellite view. Alang is the site of a huge shipbreaking yard, where obsolete ships are scrapped. Located on the southwestern shore of the Gulf of Khambhat, about 13 km (8 mi) southwest of Alang. Site open, tower closed. Operator: DGLL. ARLHS IND-123; Admiralty F0446; NGA 28188.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-123</SimpleData>
