		<SimpleData name="record">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-12/dj18.pdf</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-jamnagar/gopnath-lighthouse-dgps-station</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1975 (station established 1879). Active; focal plane 44 m (144 ft); three white flashes every 20 s. 30 m (98 ft) square cylindrical masonry tower with lantern and gallery, painted with horizontal red and white bands (the rear of the tower is all white). Rahul Kambad's 2023 photo is at right, Sohil Sarkazi has a 2010 photo, Wikimedia has a view, and Google has a 2023 street view and a satellite view. In 2021 a 3-story building was built around the tower and opened as a maritime museum; Vijay Parmar's 2021 photo shows the building under construction and Kambad's 2023 photo at right shows it completed. The new lighthouse is 500 m (0.4 mi) north of the old one. There are beach resorts in the vic</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-135</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/J-17.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:Ledger header reads 'East Island Lighthouse and DGPS Station' but postal address is Gopnath Lighthouse &amp; DGPS station,NAIS marked NA but Base Station lists 'R-40 02 Nos' and a NAIS PSS inverter is listed,Station named DGPS station but ledger has no DGPS section)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ &quot;racon&quot;: 2004 }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_since">{ &quot;racon&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2004, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;ledger&quot; }, &quot;dgps&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2003, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;network&quot; } }</SimpleData>
