		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1970 (station established 1870). Active; focal plane 45 m (148 ft); white flash every 10 s. 9 m (30 ft) square masonry tower with lantern and gallery. Lighthouse painted white with red trim; lantern dome painted red. Chetan Raval has a 2018 closeup photo and Google has a satellite view. The original light was a small lantern atop a fort built by the prince of Bhavnagar; the present lighthouse stands on the ruins of the same fort. Located on a bluff about 8 km (5 mi) southwest of the Gopnath Point lighthouse. Site open, tower closed. Operator: DGLL. ARLHS IND-140; Admiralty F0442; NGA 28196.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-140</SimpleData>
