		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1985 (station established 1877). Active; focal plane 37 m (121 ft); two white flashes every 20 s. 35 m (115 ft) hexagonal concrete tower with lantern and gallery, painted with horizontal red and white bands. The lighthouse also has an observation room at the watch room level, plus a control center encircling the middle of the tower. Lighthouse painted with horizontal red and white bands. A 2009 photo and a closeup photo (2/3 the way down the page) are available and Google has a satellite view. The original light was on a mast; it was moved in 1980 atop the port administration building. Located about 300 m from the beach and 500 m (0.3 mi) east of the waterfront in Mangrol. Site open, tower c</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-147</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/J-6.jpg</SimpleData>
