		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-jamnagar/jegri-island-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1960 (station established 1871). Active; focal plane 57 m (187 ft); two white flashes every 20 s. 30 m (98 ft) square cylindrical masonry tower with lantern and gallery, painted with horizontal black and white bands. A closeup photo and a 2021 photo are available, Amit Sorathiya has a 2014 photo, Bhavin Patel has a view from the beach, and Google has a satellite view. The original light was mounted on the keeper's house. Jegri is a small island just off the coast at Mahuva, linked to the mainland by a bridge. Located on a high bluff at the south point of the island; accessible by road. Site open, tower closed. Operator: DGLL. ARLHS IND-139; Admiralty F0438; NGA 28200.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-139</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/J-14.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(5:Name printed as 'JEGARI LIGHTHOUSE' in header; postal address says 'Jegri Lighthouse',Duration of Flash given as 1.86 Sec but characteristic sequence gives 0.3 s flashes,Effective beam intensity printed with irregular grouping '33,4,480 Candela'; read as 334480,RACON heading says '- NA-' but a Tide Land Sea Beacon System 6, code G, X &amp; S band, Oct-2005 is listed (identical to Dwarka ledger entry),NAIS lists only base station 'PSS Dwarka' with no model/MMSI)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ &quot;racon&quot;: 2005 }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_since">{ &quot;racon&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2005, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;ledger&quot; } }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="tenders">(0:)</SimpleData>
