		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1982 (station established 1965). Active; focal plane 36 m (118 ft); white flash every 7 s. 34 m (112 ft) square cylindrical concrete tower with lantern and double gallery, painted with horizontal red and white bands. The design of the present lighthouse is unusual; the light is supported by four square concrete pillars, with the stairway exposed between them. Bhushan Parab has a 2018 photo, Emil Roshal has a 2021 closeup, and Google has a 2022 street view and a satellite view as well as a distant street view from the nearby beach. The first lighthouse was a skeletal tower. Located at the south end of a barrier island about 25 km (15 mi) west of Navsari. Accessible by road. Site open, tower c</SimpleData>
