		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1965 (station established 1865). Active; focal plane 33 m (108 ft); white light occulting once every 15 s. 30 m (98 ft) cylindrical concrete tower, D-shaped in cross section, with lantern and gallery, rising from a 1-story control center. Lighthouse painted with horizontal black and white bands. Ram Vadher's 2022 photo is at right, Ravi Bhagat has a photo, a 2010 photo and another view are available, Lightphotos.net has a closeup photo, and Google has a satellite view. The two-tier lantern carries powerful lights in both Fresnel lenses. Veraval is one of the most important ports for the fishing fleets of Gujarat, so this light station has always been an important one. In 2021 the name of Ver</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-166</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q135512476</SimpleData>
