		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-jamnagar/savaibet-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1967. Active; focal plane 45 m (148 ft); four white flashes every 30 s. 27 m (89 ft) square cylindrical masonry tower with lantern and gallery, painted with horizontal red and white bands. Abhishek Srivastava's 2020 photo is at the top of this page, Jeetesh Muchhadia has a photo, Rizvan Khan has a more distant view, and Google has a satellite view. Savaibet is a small island separated from the larger island of Shialbet by a narrow channel at high tide. Located about 25 km (15 mi) east of Jafarabad. Accessible only by boat. Site and tower closed. Operator: DGLL. ARLHS IND-164; Admiralty F0436; NGA 28204.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-164</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/J-12.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
