		<SimpleData name="rowlett">2003 (station established 1901). Active; focal plane 34 m (112 ft); white flash every 10 s. 30 m (98 ft) square skeletal tower, painted with red and white horizontal bands. This tower replaced a concrete post mounted on a 1-story square concrete equipment room; this small beacon may survive. A very distant view is available and Google has a satellite view and a distant street view. The red and white concrete tower shown on the DGLL page is the Diu Head lighthouse placed here in error. The original light was mounted on the old Portuguese fort of Simar, nearby. Located on the waterfront in Simar, a small fishing port 12 km (7.5 mi) southeast of Una. Site open, tower closed. Operator: DGLL. ARL</SimpleData>
