		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1920 (station established 1896). Active; focal plane 27 m (89 ft); four white flashes every 12 s. 15 m (49 ft) round cylindrical masonry tower with lantern and gallery. Lighthouse painted white; lantern roof is red. Seta Ayaj has the 2021 photo at right and Google has a distant street view and a satellite view. We need accurate information on the history of this station. The Jenkins 1904 light list says the first light was a pillar on a rock off the point. This light is easily confused with the Navibandar Light in southwestern Gujarat; that light is listed near the bottom of this page. The two lighthouses are twins, increasing the chance of confusion. Located on a promontory about 12 km (7.5</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-156</SimpleData>
