		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1969 (station established 1882). Active; focal plane 59 m (194 ft); white flash every 10 s. 37 m (121 ft) hexagonal masonry tower with lantern and gallery, painted with horizontal red and white bands. Sanjay Dhapa's 2024 photo is at right, Chandrapal Lodhari has a 2017 photo, Vipul Baria has a 2020 photo, Vijay Dalki has a distant view, and Google has a satellite view. Diu Head is the southernmost point of Saurashtra, making this a crucial light for shipping along the coast. Located on a promontory on the west entrance to Madhvad Bay, about 4 km (2.5 mi) west of Diu Island. The promontory is accessible from the mainland by a mile-long causeway. Site open, tower open for climbing Friday throu</SimpleData>
