		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-mumbai/valsad-khadi-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">2018 (station established 1866). Active; focal plane 32 m (105 ft); four white flashes every 20 s. 30 m (98 ft) round cylindrical concrete tower with lantern, a round observation room, and two galleries. Lighthouse painted with red and white spiral bands. Kartik Tandel has a photo of the old and new lighthouses (also seen at right), Karun Patel has a 2023 photo, and Vinit Shah has a closeup photo. Khadi is a Hindi word for &quot;connection,&quot; here meaning the inlet from the sea. Located about 2 km (1.25 mi) south of the mouth of the Auranga River, 8 km (5 mi) west of Valsad. Accessible by road. Site open, tower open late afternoons daily. Operator: DGLL. ARLHS IND-172; Admiralty F0480; NGA 28108.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-172</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/Valsad_Khadi_Lighthouse.png</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
