		<SimpleData name="ledger_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/kalkata%206.pdf</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-kolkata/puri-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">2002 (station established 1887). Active; focal plane 29 m (95 ft); three white flashes every 20 s. 25 m (82 ft) round cylindrical concrete tower with lantern and double gallery, painted with horizontal black and white bands. Several 1-story keeper's cottages nearby. Amit Dey's 2024 photo is at right, Suprriya Basak has a 2022 photo, Aditya Biswaman has a 2017 closeup, Tamal Guha has a late evening street view from the beach, and Google has a satellite view. This is by far the best known lighthouse of Odisha. Early lights were mounted on the wall of the Circuit House; in 1956 a skeletal tower was mounted atop a new Circuit House. The Puri area is a very popular seaside resort; H.G. Mukhopadhy</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-056</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:Elevation given as 'Elevation of ground 5.2 m' and 'Elevation of tower 30.2 m'; 30.2 m used,Divergence values printed without units,Year of establishment not stated)</SimpleData>
