		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-mumbai/arnala-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">2019 (station established 1860). Active; focal plane 33 m (108 ft); three flashes every 15 s, white or red depending on direction. 30 m (98 ft) round concrete tower with lantern and double gallery, painted with black and white spiral bands. Emmanuel Dinis has a 2022 closeup photo, Nitin Bhoir has a 2023 photo, Mahendra Kharpade has a March 2020 view from the sea and Google has a satellite view of the new tower. There's a closeup late 2019 YouTube video of the new tower and its 1996 predecessor, a square skeletal tower with double gallery painted white. The older tower was demolished. The original light on a mast was replaced by skeletal towers in 1907 and again in 1967. Located in Arnala, a </SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-074</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/Arnala%20Lighthouse.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(4:Colour given as 'WR' with no sector bearings,No. of lens '08 ( 06 In sevies)' is unclear,Duration of Flash field reads '15 Sec , 2rpm'; 2 rpm with 8 lenses does not obviously match 3 flashes per 15 s,RACON and NAIS sections are blank tables)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_since">{ }</SimpleData>
