		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1960. Active; focal plane 53 m (174 ft); two white flashes every 15 s. Approx. 17 m (56 ft) square cylindrical masonry tower with lantern and gallery, painted with horizontal red and white bands and attached to a 1-story keeper's house. Ambert Miranda has the 2021 photo seen below right, Pravin Ubhare has a photo, Amar Kumar has a 2011 photo, and Google has a satellite view. Located near the northwestern point of Salsette Island, about 50 km (30 mi) north of Mumbai. Accessible by road. Site open, tower closed. ARLHS IND-119; Admiralty F0499; NGA 28060.</SimpleData>
