		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-kolkata/gopalpur-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1967 (station established 1871). Active; focal plane 48 m (148 ft); white flash every 5 s. 32 m (105 ft) round masonry tower with lantern and gallery, attached to several 1-story keeper's houses. Lighthouse painted with horizontal red and white bands. Narasingh Naik's 2022 photo is at right, a good closeup photo is available, Purnima Roy has a more distant view, Umashankar Behera has a street view from the beach, and Google has a satellite view. The original mast light was replaced by a skeletal tower in 1925; a second skeletal tower was built in 1948. Gopalpur-on-Sea is also a very popular seaside resort, and this is one of the three lighthouses in Odisha designated for tourist development </SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-035</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:Elevation given as 'Elevation of ground 8 m' and 'Elevation of tower 45 m'; 45 m used,Divergence values printed without units,Year of establishment not stated)</SimpleData>
