		<SimpleData name="rowlett">2012 (station establishment date unknown). Active; focal plane 30 m (98 ft); two white flashes every 15 s. 30 m (98 ft) octagonal cylindrical concrete tower with lantern and gallery, painted with black and white horizontal bands; lantern painted red. Biman Sahu has a closeup, Shubham Kumar has a 2025 photo, Raju Pydi has a 2022 photo, and Google has a satellite view. The previous light was mounted &quot;on port flagstaff,&quot; according to NGA, although there does not appear to be an active port at Baruva. This light was deactivated in 2003 and there was no light until the new lighthouse was activated. An 1889 Bay of Bengal Pilot describes an unlit &quot;column,&quot; painted with black and white bands, at Bar</SimpleData>
