		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-mumbai/prongs-reef-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1874 (British; lightship station established 1842). Active; focal plane 41 m (135 ft); white flash every 10 s. 44 m (144 ft) round tapered stone tower with lantern and two galleries, mounted on a stone pier. 1st order Fresnel lens in use. The tower is painted white with a red horizontal band, and the supporting pier is painted black. A 2023 photo is at right, Milan Vyas has a 2021 photo, Mayur Mangela has a photo, Sahil Chauhan has a 2022 photo, Trabas has Cameron's 2010 view, a view from shore is available, Huelse has a historic postcard image, and Google has a good satellite view. This historic offshore lighthouse, marking the entrance to Mumbai Harbour, replaced the onshore Colaba Point l</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-007</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q16956772</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/Prongs%20reef%20Lighthouse.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(4:R.P.M. given as 1 but rotation device says speed selectable from 0.5-0.6 RPM,Range '23' printed without unit or luminous/geographical label,Date of commissioning lists both 1875 and 29.06.2008 (taken over from Mumbai Port Trust 11.10.2007),Standby NA yet a portable Honda 2.5KVA generator is listed)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_since">{ &quot;racon&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2004, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;network&quot; } }</SimpleData>
