		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1982 (station established 1877). Active; focal plane 35 m (115 ft); three white flashes every 15 s. 30 m (98 ft) hexagonal cylindrical masonry tower with lantern and gallery, painted with horizontal red and white bands. Nilakantha Mahapatra has a closeup 2024 photo, Gowtham Kambhampati has a 2016 photo, Muni Raja Bonthala has a 2018 photo, Wikimedia has photos, and Google has a satellite view. Located at Kalingapatnam, a beach resort town about 30 km (19 mi) east of Srikakulam at the mouth of the Vamsadhara River. Accessible by road. Site open, tower status unknown. . ARLHS IND-036; Admiralty F0982; NGA 26956.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-036</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q30039442</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Kalingapatnam%20light%20house%2003.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
