		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-vishakhapatnam/santapalli-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1903 British; (station established 1840). Active; focal plane 43 m (141 ft); two white flashes every 10 s. 22 m (72 ft) round masonry tower with lantern and gallery, painted with horizontal black and white bands; lantern dome painted red. Aditya Vishnu Vardhan Inuganti's 2022 photo is at right, Dayal Saran has a closeup 2016 photo, Kartheek Dummu has a 2019 photo, and the lighthouse and several station buildings are seen in a Google satellite view. The original light, a temporary structure on the beach, was destroyed by a typhoon. Ruins of the second (1849) lighthouse, which had a light tower attached to a keeper's house, can also be seen. According to DGLL remains of a primitive 18th centur</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-061</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q57518237</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/Santapalli%20Lighthouse.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(4:Sequence (0.2+2.3+0.2+7) sums to 9.7 s but period stated as 10 s,Horizontal divergence printed as '6° 45 6'' (ambiguous, possibly 6° 45.6'),Estd./year of first light 1840 but Date of Commissioning given as 1903,ALOL given only as Sr.No. '0980' without letter prefix)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ &quot;ais&quot;: 2011 }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_since">{ &quot;ais&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2011, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;ledger&quot; } }</SimpleData>
