		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1903 (British). Active; focal plane 12 m (39 ft); white flash every 9 s. 11 m (36 ft) masonry tower, painted white. A 2017 photo is at right, Matt Kutsch also has a good photo, Laxmi Saha has a 2022 photo, and Google has a satellite view. In January 2013 it was announced that this historic lighthouse would be demolished and replaced, but these plans were dropped. Google's January 2017 street view shows the old tower very much in place, with visitors on the gallery. In March 2022 government officials visited to survey sites for a new lighthouse; it would have a height of about 30 m (100 ft). Located near the port office in Bhimunipatnam (Bheemili), a seaport at the mouth of the river Gosthani</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-023</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/Bheemlipatnam%20Lighthouse.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:Name printed as 'BHEEMINIPATNAM LIGHT HOUSE' in the Name field; page title reads 'Bheemlipatnam Lighthouse',Latitude printed as 17° 56'.30&quot; (mixed minute/second notation); converted as 17°56'30&quot;,Duration of flash given as 0.38 seconds but characteristic sequence gives FL 1 s)</SimpleData>
