		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-mumbai/harnai-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1899 (British). Active; focal plane 29 m (95 ft); red flash every 5 s. 10 m (33 ft) round concrete tower with gallery; the lantern has been replaced by a light on a short mast. The lighthouse was formerly painted white, but in photos it seems most of the paint has weathered off. Amit Kulkarni has a 2023 photo, Jagannath Sahoo has a 2024 photo, Khalil Sawant has a 2008 closeup photo, and Google has a satellite view. Located atop a narrow promontory, connected to the mainland by a causeway, on the north side of the harbor entrance at Harnai. Site probably open, tower closed. ARLHS IND-086; Admiralty F0564; NGA 27904.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-086</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/Harnai%20Lighthouse.jpg</SimpleData>
