		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-vishakhapatnam/dolphin-nose-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1957 (station established 1874). Active; focal plane 173 m (568 ft); white flash every 10 s. 15 m (49 ft) square cylindrical masonry tower with lantern and gallery, painted with horizontal black and white bands; lantern dome painted red. Joel Lava's 2024 photo is at the top of this page, Jaydip Bhattacharya has a 2017 closeup photo, Pallab Ghosh also has a photo, the lighthouse can be seen atop the rock in a distant view of the headland, and Google has a satellite view of the station. A light was displayed at the nearby fort as early as 1874, but there was no proper lighthouse until about 1905. The first lighthouse at the present site was built in 1940. The Dolphin's Nose is a huge rocky hea</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-032</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q57499110</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Dolphin%27s%20Nose%20Lighthouse%20-%20panoramio.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(4:Elevation printed as '173 above MSL' without unit,Luminous range printed as '32 M' (unit presumably NM),1 panel at 3 RPM gives one flash every 20 s, but characteristic is Fl every 10 s,Year of first light 1940; present lighthouse commissioned 15-06-1957)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ &quot;racon&quot;: 2005, &quot;navtex&quot;: 2015 }</SimpleData>
