		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-mumbai/tolkeshwar-point-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1958 (station established 1880). Active; focal plane 104 m (341 ft); three white flashes every 15 s. 14 m (46 ft) square cylindrical masonry tower with lantern and gallery, painted white; lantern dome painted red. Vitthal Kemble has a closeup 2022 photo, Ranjit Wagh has a 2017 photo, Praveen Jadhav has a closeup photo, Nilesh Korgaonkar reports on a 1998 visit, and Google has a satellite view of the station. The original cast iron post light was replaced by a short masonry tower in 1934. Located on a high promontory near Dabhol, about 20 km (13 mi) north northwest of Guhagar. Site open, tower open daily 3 to 5 pm. ARLHS IND-117; Admiralty F0566; NGA 27888.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-117</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/Tolkeshwar%20Point%20Lighthouse.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
