		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1991 (station established 1971). Active; focal plane 35 m (115 ft); two white flashes every 15 s. 26 m (85 ft) square cylindrical masonry tower with lantern and gallery, painted with horizontal red and white bands. A 2019 photo by Dommeti Venkata Mahesh at right, Yajjala Mahesh has a 2022 photo, Sivakodandarao Yeripalli has a 2017 photo, a closeup photo is available, and Google has a satellite view. The history of this station is not clear but apparently the present tower was built in 1991. Located on a sandy promontory at Pudi Madaka, about 55 km (35 mi) southwest of Vishakhapatnam. Site open, tower open daily. . ARLHS IND-054; Admiralty F0968; NGA 27012.</SimpleData>
