		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-vishakhapatnam/vakalapudi-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">2005 (station established 1868). Active; focal plane 45 m (148 ft); three white flashes every 15 s. 45 m (148 ft) round cylindrical masonry tower with lantern and double gallery. Lighthouse painted with horizontal red and white bands. Bhuvan Eswar's 2022 photo is at right, Thyaga Raju has a photo of both Vakalapudi lighthouses, there's a closeup of the top of the tower, and Google has a satellite view. This lighthouse marks the mainland side of the entrance to the bay of Kakinada, which is sheltered by a long, curving sand spit. Located at Vakalapudi about 12 km (7.5 mi) north of Kakinada. Site open, tower open in late afternoons. . ARLHS IND-064; Admiralty F0964; NGA 27020.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-064</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q57500037</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/Vakalapudi%20Lighthouse.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:Luminous range printed '26 M' (unit not NM),Header says Estd.1878 but year of first light given as 2004 (taken over from Port Department of Andhra Pradesh), commissioning 08-11-2004,ALOL printed '0964' without letter prefix)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ &quot;racon&quot;: 2004, &quot;ais&quot;: 2011, &quot;navtex&quot;: 2015 }</SimpleData>
