		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1965 (station established 1867). Active; focal plane 102 m (335 ft); two white flashes every 10 s. 15 m (49 ft) round masonry tower with lantern and gallery, painted with black and white horizontal bands; lantern dome painted red. Shantaram Gadiyar has a 2024 photo, Kristina Hoeppner' has a 2007 photo, Akash Bhise has a 2018 photo, and Google has a satellite view. The original lighthouse, a 10 m (33 ft) masonry tower, was replaced by a skeletal tower in 1940. The lighthouse is within the walls of Ratnagiri Fort. Located on heights on the south side of the harbor at Ratnagiri. Accessible by road. Site open, tower open for tours daily 4 to 5 pm. ARLHS IND-110; Admiralty F0580; NGA 27856.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-110</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/Ratnagiri%20Town%20and%20DGPS%20Station.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
