		<SimpleData name="rowlett">Date unknown (station established 1895). Active; focal plane 43 m (141 ft); white flash every 5 s. 45 m (148 ft) round cylindrical concrete tower with lantern and gallery. Tower painted with red and white horizontal bands; lantern dome painted red. A 2021 photo of the two towers is at right, Ampilli Sathvik has a 2024 photo of the two towers, Sai Charan has a 2018 photo of the two towers, a 2017 photo of the station is available, and Google has a good satellite view. This is one of the tallest lighthouses of India; it marks a sandy cape south of the mouth of the Vrudha Godavari, the northernmost mouth of the river. The Sacramento lighthouses replaced the former Cape Godavery lighthouses, as </SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-059</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q57518421</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/Sacramento%20Lighthouse.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(4:Luminous range printed as '24 andelas' (unit garbled); taken as 24 NM,Horizontal divergence printed '6° 45 5'' is ambiguous (6°45.5' or 6°45'5&quot;); left null,Header says 'Estd.1985/2015' but Date of Commissioning is 1895 (innovations 1902, 1997, 2004, 17-02-2015),Duration of flash given as 0.19 seconds vs characteristic Fl 0.2)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ &quot;ais&quot;: 2016 }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_since">{ &quot;ais&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2016, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;ledger&quot; } }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="tenders">(1:868)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo_credit">DGLL</SimpleData>
	</SchemaData></ExtendedData>
