		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1958 (station established 1915). Active; focal plane 42 m (138 ft); four white flashes every 23 s. 11 m (36 ft) round masonry tower with lantern and gallery, painted with black and white horizontal bands; lantern dome painted red. A radar antenna is mounted atop the lighthouse. Prashant Kesarkar's 2023 photo is at right, Pandurang Bhise has a 2019 closeup photo, Atharva Kubal has a 2025 closeup, Yash Talekar has a 2018 photo, Kothanda Srinivasan also has a photo, and Google has a satellite view. The lighthouse is built within the walls of a ruined early 18th century fortress. Located on a promontory at south side of the harbor entrance at Devgad, about 80 km (50 mi) north of Vengurla. Site o</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-084</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/DEVGAD%20LIGHTHOUSE.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(2:No. of lens 4 (each of 60°) with 4 lenses totalling 240°,Solar Plant row says NA while 'Solar Plant for Main' lists 200W x2 and 190W x1 panels)</SimpleData>
