		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1971. Active; focal plane 29 m (95 ft); two white flashes every 15 s.26 m (85 ft) square cylindrical masonry tower with lantern and gallery, painted with horizontal red and white bands. 4th order clamshell Fresnel lens in use. Manik Sehgal has a 2019 photo, Ganesh Maddula has a 2018 photo, a 2023 closeup is available, Arjun Am has a distant street view from the beach, Suresh Tirumani has a street view from the gallery, and Google has a satellite view. Located on Narsapur Point on the east side of the mouth of the Vasishta Godavari, the southern branch of the Godavari, about 20 km (13 mi) south of Narsapur (Narasapuram). Site open, tower open in the afternoons. . ARLHS IND-021; Admiralty F095</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-021</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q57518490</SimpleData>
