		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-goa/achara-point-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">2014. Active; focal plane 49 m (161 ft); two white flashes every 6 s. 17 m (56 ft) round concrete tower with lantern and gallery. Lighthouse painted white, lantern roof red. Abhay Aparaj has a 2019 photo and a closeup of this new lighthouse, Nikhil Karangutkar has a 2022 photo, Jayanti Dhuri has a very distant view and Google has a satellite view. NGA lists a 9 m (30 ft) skeletal tower at this location, and an Indian Notice to Mariners identified that light as &quot;temporarily extinguished&quot; in 2012. Located on a steep headland across the estuary entrance at Achra, a village about 50 km (30 mi) north of Vengurla. Site status unknown. Admiralty F0592; NGA 27832.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/ACHARA%20POINT%20LIGHTHOUSE.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:Duration of flash given as '06 Sec', same as the period; not a plausible flash duration, not transcribed as flash_duration_s,RACON Sr. No 6295 listed but all RACON details NA,Solar plant shown under 'Solar Plant for Main RACON' although RACON is NA; 'Mains' row describes a solar battery bank)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_since">{ }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="tenders">(0:)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo_credit">DGLL</SimpleData>
	</SchemaData></ExtendedData>
      <Point><coordinates>73.43167,16.2</coordinates></Point>
