		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-goa/vengurla-rocks-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1890 (British; station established 1870). Active; focal plane 49 m (161 ft); two white flashes every 20 s. 21 m (69 ft) round cast iron tower with lantern and gallery, painted with red and white horizontal bands. A 2021 photo is at right, Lighthouse Digest has a photo, Rajesh Prabhu has a 2022 photo, Kaina Shaikh has a 2022 aerial photo, Bhushan Parab has a view from the sea, an Instagram photo is available, and Google has a satellite view. Located in the Arabian Sea about 11 km (7 mi) off the coast and 20 km (13 mi) west northwest of Vengurla. Accessible only by boat and landing appears difficult or impossible. Site and tower closed. ARLHS IND-009; Admiralty F0598; NGA 27804.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-009</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/Vengurla%20Rocks%20Lighthouse.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(4:Position and divergence printed with '*' in place of degree signs,Date of commissioning not stated ('-'),RACON Sr. No 6295 is the same serial printed in other ledgers (Anjengo, Minicoy),NAIS section lists only VSAT/modem, no AIS base station details)</SimpleData>
