		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1902. Active; focal plane 85 m (279 ft); three white flashes every 20 s. 21 m (69 ft) square concrete tower with lantern and gallery, painted white; lantern roof painted red. Kamal Irukulla's 2022 photo is at right, Nasa Anil Kumar has a 2021 photo, a 2009 photo is available, Swechha Prakash has a street view, and Google has a satellite view. Apparently this light was built originally as the front light of a range, with the old lighthouse (previous entry) as the rear light. It is not known when the range was discontinued. Located a short distance west of Fort Aguada. Site open, tower open daily 10 am to 5:30 pm. ARLHS IND-069; Admiralty F0606; NGA 27772.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-069</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q10280110</SimpleData>
