		<SimpleData name="rowlett">2015 (station established 1890). Active; focal plane 88 m (289 ft); white flash every 15 s. Approx. 21 m (69 ft) octagonal cylindrical concrete tower with lantern and gallery, painted with red and white spiral bands. A 2022 photo is at right, Bikash Pradhan has a 2016 photo, Conroy Rodrigues has a second 2016 photo, Viresh Vazirani has a gallery view from atop the tower, Ashwin Sekhar has a street view, and Google has a satellite view. Located atop a steep hill behind Betul Beach southwest of Margao. Site open, tower open in late afternoons daily. . Admiralty F0631; NGA 27758.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/BETUL%20LIGHTHOUSE.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(6:Characteristic says FL4 (W) 15S but Duration of Flash field says 'Flash (1) white 15 sec',Latitude printed in mixed format (15° 08’.41.7”); interpreted as 15° 08' 41.7&quot;,No. of lens given as '3 tyre 3 panel (each panel 3 led lights)',Divergence 2.5 degrees not labelled horizontal or vertical,Effective beam intensity blank,RACON lists only Sr. No 6295 with no make/model/code)</SimpleData>
