		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-vishakhapatnam/ramayapatnam-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">2005 (station established 1982). Active; focal plane 34 m (112 ft); white flash every 10 s. 35 m (115 ft) hexagonal cylindrical concrete tower with lantern and gallery, painted with horizontal red and white bands. Ramesh Pagidipalli has a 2023 photo, Yespear Kay has a photo, Chaitanya Ramireddy has a 2020 closeup, Kiran Darling has a street view from the gallery, and Google has a satellite view. This lighthouse and the next several to the south stand on the northern Coromandel Coast, a low shore devastated by the great tsunami of 26 December 2004. There was a news report that the &quot;oldest lighthouse at Ramayapatnam&quot; collapsed in the waves; presumably this was the 1982 tower. Located at Ramaya</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-057</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q57517972</SimpleData>
