		<SimpleData name="ledger_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-12/Master%20Ledger%20Goa%2014.pdf</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-goa/oyster-rocks-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1864 (British). Active; focal plane 63 m (207 ft); white flash every 10 s. 19 m (62 ft) round masonry tower with lantern and gallery, painted red with one white horizontal band; lantern painted white with a red dome. 2nd order Fresnel lens. Sachin Kuvalekar's 2018 photo is at right, Nitya Juvekar has a 2018 closeup photo, a 2022 closeup is available, Kaushik Saikia has a distant view at dusk, and Google has a satellite view. This is the oldest lighthouse of Karnataka, built by the British to support their new outpost at Karwar following the Indian Mutiny uprising of 1857. The Oyster Rocks are the westernmost of several reefs and islets protecting the harbor of Karwar. Located about 8 km (5 m</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-105</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q7116356</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/The%20Oyster%20Rocks%20lighthouse.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:No. of lens '2 (each 144°)',Area of dioptric portion 5124 sq. cm but 'corrected area 38880 sq.cm' is larger,Date of commissioning given only as year 1934)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ &quot;racon&quot;: 2005 }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_since">{ &quot;racon&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2005, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;ledger&quot; }, &quot;ais&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2012, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;network&quot; } }</SimpleData>
