		<SimpleData name="rowlett">Date unknown. Active; focal plane 30 m (98 ft); two white flashes every 10 s. 9 m (30 ft) hexagonal cylindrical concrete tower with lantern and gallery centered on a round 2-story base. Entire lighthouse painted with black and white horizontal bands. Srinivasan Arumugam has a 2018 closeup photo, Sharath Kharvi has a 2020 closeup photo, Wikimapia has photos, Devdas Kharvi has a 2020 street view, and Google has a 2023 street view and an indistinct satellite view. The lighthouse honors Tipu (or Tippu) Sultan, the ruler of Mysore from 1782 to 1799. Located on the beachfront about 4 km (2.5 mi) north of the estuary entrance at Kundapura. Site open, tower closed. Operator: Karnataka Maritime Board</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/KUNDAPUR%20LIGHTHOUSE.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:Optic Make and Type values appear swapped (Make: 'WM – RB 500 Marine Rotating Beacon', Type: 'Wealth Marine Pvt. Ltd., Singapore'),No. of lens '6 (4 Fresnellens + 2 blanks)': 6 panel positions, only 4 lenses,RACON marked n/a but Sr. No 6295 listed)</SimpleData>
