		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-chennai/pulicat-lighthouse-and-dgps-station</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1986 (station established 1862). Active; focal plane 53 m (174 ft); white flash every 5 s. 49 m (160 ft) hexagonal cylindrical concrete tower with lantern and gallery, painted with horizontal black and white bands. Anandha Rajan's 2025 photo is at right, Manas Karkal has a 2023 photo, Vasant Viswanathan has a good photo, Jeevan Kumar has a photo, John Peter has a street view, and Google has a satellite view. In January 2014 the lighthouse was opened to visitors for the first time. Pulicat Lake is a large lagoon on the border between Andhra Pradesh and Tamil Nadu. Pulicat (Pazhaverkadu), on the south side of the lagoon entrance, was settled by the Portuguese in 1502. Captured by the Dutch in </SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-055</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/dg1.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(2:Elevation printed as '53.5M (49.86 Mtrs. Above MSL)' and tower height as '49.86 Metres above MSL (53.5 Meters elevation)'; figures are contradictory,Divergence fields are blank)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ &quot;racon&quot;: 2004, &quot;ais&quot;: 2019 }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_since">{ &quot;racon&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2004, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;ledger&quot; }, &quot;ais&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2019, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;ledger&quot; }, &quot;dgps&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2003, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;network&quot; } }</SimpleData>
