		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1973 (station established 1901). Active; focal plane 29 m (95 ft); white flash every 3 s. Approx. 12 m (39 ft) square cylindical masonry tower with lantern and gallery, painted white. Two 1-story keeper's houses. A photo showing both lighthouses (1/5 the way down the page) and a view from the sea are available and Google has a satellite view. Jayalal Udupi has a pier view of the island in which the tower can just be seen. Located atop an island southwest of the entrance to the harbor of Malpe. Accessible only by boat. Site status unknown. ARLHS IND-098; Admiralty F0655; NGA 27708.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-098</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/Malpe%20Lighthouse.jpg</SimpleData>
