		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1901 (British). Active; focal plane 43 m (141 ft); three white flashes every 20 s. 27 m (89 ft) round masonry tower with lantern and gallery, painted with black and white horizontal bands; lantern dome painted red. Vignesh Poojary's photo is at right, Kishan Kusagur has a 2022 closeup, Nishant Nadar has a 2020 photo, Nagaraj V. Gowda has a closeup, Anita Bora has a 2005 photo, Huelse has a historic postcard view, Krishna Acharya has a beach view, and Google has a satellite view. This is easily the best known lighthouse of Karnataka. In December 2021 district officials announced plans for visitor improvements including a paved path and viewing platform. Located on a low but rocky promontory i</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-091</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q29959903</SimpleData>
