		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-chennai/chennai-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1977 (station established 1796). Active; focal plane 57 m (187 ft); two white flashes every 10 s. 46 m (151 ft) pentagonal cylindrical concrete tower with lantern and double gallery, attached to a 3-story circular harbor control building. The two seaward sides of the lighthouse are painted with horizontal red and white bands. A 2023 photo by Venkata Lokesh is at right, Trabas has Eckhard Meyer's 2008 photo, Kelly Cheng also has a photo, R. Srijith has a view from the beach, Wikimedia has several photos, and Google has a 2022 street view and a satellite view. Waves from the great tsunami of 26 December 2004 damaged the base of the lighthouse, but there were no casualties. The lighthouse reope</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-010</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q6546309</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/dg23.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:Headline says Group Flash (2) every 2 sec but sequence 0.57+1.93+0.57+6.93 sums to 10 s,Duration of Flash (Main) printed as '10 sec', inconsistent with 0.57 s flashes in the sequence,Luminous range given for two atmospheric transmission factors (A.T.F. 0.74 @ 22 NM, A.T.F. 0.84 @ 35 NM); 22 NM used)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ &quot;racon&quot;: 2010 }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_since">{ &quot;racon&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2010, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;ledger&quot; }, &quot;ais&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2012, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;network&quot; } }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="tenders">(6:2241,1967,1921,1900,1719,1596)</SimpleData>
