		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1972. Active; focal plane 44 m (144 ft); white flash every 10 s. 36 m (118 ft) square cylindrical concrete tower with lantern and gallery, painted with red and white horizontal bands. 2-story keeper's house adjacent or attached to the lighthouse. A 2021 photo is at right, another good photo is available, Raghavendra Joshi has a 2018 photo, Wikimedia has a photo, P. Bachodi has a distant photo, Sandeep Nayak has a beach view, and Google has a satellite view. Standing by a very popular beach, this lighthouse functions as the landfall light for Mangalore. In 2020 DGLL approved plans to renovate the lighthouse as a tourist attraction. Located off the beach about 8 km (5 mi) north of Suratkal and</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-114</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/Surathkal%20Lighthouse%20and%20D.G.P.S%20Station.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:Longitude printed without hemisphere letter; taken as E,NAIS MMSI printed as 4192237 (7 digits, not the usual 9),DGPS: NAUTEL, 320, 500, RS IDs 412/413, Beacon ID 106, commissioned 06/05/1998, recapitalised 22/06/2017)</SimpleData>
