		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1900 (British; station established 1887). Active; focal plane 42 m (138 ft); white flash every 10 s. 26 m (85 ft) round stone tower with lantern and gallery; unpainted; lantern dome painted red. 2nd order Fresnel lens in use. Ali Akbar's 2024 photo is at the top of this page, Srini Swaminathan has a closeup photo, Trabas has a 2014 photo by Alfonso Biescas Vignau, Wikimedia has numerous photos, Asharul Seikh has a 2021 photo, Forand has a historic postcard view, Huelse has a closeup postcard view, and Google has a street view and a satellite view. This is probably the best known and most often visited lighthouse on India's east coast. In 2013 it was one of the first lighthouses in India iden</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-016</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q18127656</SimpleData>
