		<SimpleData name="rowlett">2013. Active; focal plane 36 m (118 ft); three white flashes every 20 s. 32 m (105 ft) round cylindrical concrete tower with lantern, gallery, and a round observation platform. Lighthouse painted with red and white spiral bands. Prem Kumar has a 2016 photo, V. Saravanan has a distant view, Sandeep Jinnu has a closeup 2019 photo, and Google has a 2023 street view and a satellite view. The lighthouse was placed in service in November 2013. Located in Kadapakkam, a town about 40 km (25 mi) north of Puducherry, close to the historic (1760) Alamparai Fort. Site open, tower status unknown. Admiralty F0929; NGA 27110.</SimpleData>
