		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-kochi/mahe-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1976 (station established 1903). Active; focal plane 35 m (115 ft); white flash every 10 s. 23 m (75 ft) round concrete tower with gallery and a small lantern, painted red with one white horizontal band. A 2024 photo is at right, Mohamed Salim has a good closeup photo, Wikimedia has a photo, Lightphotos.net has a closeup, and Google has a satellite view and a 2017 street view. Kannur (formerly called Cannanore) is the largest city of North Kerala with a metropolitan population of more than 1.6 million. is The first Cannanore lighthouses were at Fort St. Angelo, an early 16th century Portuguese fort. Lanterns were shown from the fort walls as early as 1843. A permanent light was mounted on a </SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-079</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/MAHE%20LIGHTHOUSE.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(4:Ledger has no station title; postal address names 'Kannur Lighthouse, Burnacherry Post, Kannur' although file slug is mahe-lighthouse,Position printed as 11° 51’5’ / 75° 21’4’; read as degrees-minutes-seconds (could be 51.5'/21.4'),Sequence 2.04+7.94 sums to 9.98 s, not 10 s,This ledger is published on DGLL's Mahe Lighthouse page, but its address, position and light are Kannur Lighthouse's)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_since">{ }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="tenders">(4:2572,2096,2025,1880)</SimpleData>
