		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-kochi/chetlat-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1984. Active; focal plane 36 m (118 ft); three white flashes every 30 s. 30 m (98 ft) square galvanized iron skeletal tower, painted with black and white horizontal bands; there is a 1-story concrete equipment room inside the base. Google has a satellite view. Another sibling of the Amini Light. Chetlat is a small, isolated island on the northeast side of the Amindivis. Boat transportation is available about once a week from the other islands. Located by the pier on the west side of the island. Site open, tower closed. Admiralty F0749; NGA 27588.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/CHETLAT%20LIGHTHOUSE.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:Ledger never names the station; postal address and facilities refer to Kadamat Lighthouse / Kadamat Island, so this sheet may be Kadamat's data filed under Chetlat,Position minutes printed with a double-prime (&quot;) sign; treated as decimal minutes,Source of energy says 'Solar Plant: NIL' yet lists solar panels)</SimpleData>
