		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-kochi/bitra-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1984 (station established 1977). Active; focal plane 33 m (108 ft); nine quick white flashes every 10 s. 30 m (98 ft) square galvanized iron skeletal tower, painted with red and white horizontal bands; there is a 1-story concrete equipment room inside the base. The tower is hard to see in Google's satellite view. One more Amini class lighthouse. The original light was on a shorter wood skeletal tower. Bitra is a small island in a large atoll on the west side of the Amindivis. Site open, tower closed. ARLHS LAK-003; Admiralty F0750; NGA 27580.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">LAK-003</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/BITRA%20LIGHTHOUSE.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:Position minutes printed with a double-prime (&quot;) sign; treated as decimal minutes,Source of energy says 'Solar Plant: NIL' yet lists solar panels for main light and automation,Year taken from date of commissioning 07.05.1984)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ }</SimpleData>
