		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1981. Active; focal plane 36 m (118 ft); white flash every 15 s. 39 m (128 ft) round cylindrical concrete tower with lantern and double gallery, painted with horizontal red and white bands. Vinoth Kuma's 2022 photo is at right, P.C.R. Antony has a closeup photo, Hasan Shaik has a photo, and Google has a satellite view. This was another location hit badly by the tsunami of 26 December 2004. One of the keepers lost his father and his son to the tsunami. The three daughters of the head keeper were also washed away, but they were rescued by local villagers. Named by Portuguese sailors, Porto Novo (Parangipettai) is a historic European base (its Tamil name means &quot;home of the foreigners&quot;). However</SimpleData>
