		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-kochi/kiltan-lighthouse-north</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">2011 (station established 1937). Active; focal plane 16 m (52 ft); two white flashes every 15 s. 15 m (49 ft) square cylindrical brick tower with gallery, painted white. Aflal Hussain has the closeup 2022 photo at right and Google has a satellite view. The original light, shown from a 6 m (20 ft) mast atop a 9 m (30 ft) masonry base, was the only navigational light in the islands, except for the Minicoy lighthouse, until the Androth East End lighthouse was built in 1967. It was replaced in 1976 by a cylindrical white concrete tower with two galleries. Located on the beach at the extreme northern tip of the island. Site open, tower closed. ARLHS LAK-007; Admiralty F0752; NGA 27572.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">LAK-007</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/KILTAN%20LIGHTHOUSE%20%28NORTH%29.jpg</SimpleData>
