		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1988 (station established 1976). Active; focal plane 40 m (131 ft); white flash every 5 s. 38 m (125 ft) round cylindrical concrete tower with lantern and double gallery. Lighthouse painted white; lantern roof is red. A 2021 photo by Dawn Dennies is at right, Mike Prince has a closeup photo, Manish Singh has a view from the sea, M. Vijayan has a 2017 photo, Arun C. Mehta has a 2018 closeup, and Google has an indistinct satellite view. The original light was on a wood skeletal tower. Kavaratti, in the central part of the Laccadives, has been the capital of Lakshadweep since 1964. The town has a population of about 12,000. The island is accessible by passenger ferry from Cochin or by helicopte</SimpleData>
