		<SimpleData name="record">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-12/ch9.pdf</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-chennai/karaikal-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1901 (French) (station established 1853). Active; focal plane 18 m (59 ft); two white flashes every 10 s. 18 m (56 ft) round cylindrical white concrete tower with lantern and gallery. Sahib Nagore has a 2021 photo, Ameer Muhsin has a closeup 2019 photo, and Google has a satellite view. The current lantern was installed recently; Jaikumar Natarajan has a 2011 photo and Binoop Vasudevan has a 2014 photo showing that the original lantern was removed. The first lights were displayed here from a flagstaff; a masonry &quot;column&quot; was built in 1864. More than 500 fishermen from the area were killed by the tsunami of 26 December 2004. Located just off the beach at Karaikal. Site open, tower open daily. </SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-037</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q141223861</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/dg9.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:Latitude seconds printed as 99&quot; (&gt;= 60): '10° 54'99&quot; N'; converted as printed,Duration of flash given as '10 Sec', equal to the period; not transcribed as flash_duration_s,Commissioned 12.09.1992; renovated lighthouse opened 15/04/2019)</SimpleData>
