		<SimpleData name="rowlett">Early 2010s (station established 1976). Active; focal plane 35 m (115 ft) (?); three white flashes every 30 s. Approx. 23 m (75 ft) square skeletal tower, painted white. Ankur Saraf has a 2023 photo, Roshan Chauhan has a distant 2024 view, and Google has a satellite view. The first lighthouse was a 15 m (49 ft) wood skeletal tower; it was replaced in 1986 by the tower seen on the DGLL page. Located at the northeastern corner of the island. Site status unknown. ARLHS LAK-001; Admiralty F0754.7; NGA 27600.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">LAK-001</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/AGATTI%20LIGHTHOUSE.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:Characteristic printed as 'Fl (30) W 30 sec' - a group of 30 flashes is implausible, possibly a typo,Effective beam intensity fields are blank,characteristic reads Fl (30); treated as a typo, not simulated as 30 flashes)</SimpleData>
