		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1967. Active; focal plane 35 m (115 ft); two white flashes every 10 s. 33 m (108 ft) square masonry tower with lantern and gallery, painted with horizontal black and white bands. Sachin Satheesh has a 2023 closeup photo, a distant view from the sea is available, and Google has an indistinct satellite view of the lighthouse. Androth (Andrott), the easternmost island of Lakshadweep, is accessible by a weekly passenger ferry from Cochin. Located on the waterfront near the east end of the island. Site open, tower closed. ARLHS LAK-002; Admiralty F0755; NGA 27616.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">LAK-002</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/ANDROTH%20EAST%20LIGHTHOUSE.jpg</SimpleData>
