		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1983 (station established 1937). Active; focal plane 33 m (108 ft); white flash every 15 s. 30 m (98 ft) 12-sided concrete tower, painted with black and white horizontal bands. Akash Dinesh's 2024 photo is at right, John Alex has contributed a photo, S. Dhruvaraj has another good photo, a 2017 photo is available, Raheem Ponnad has a 2021 photo, Nousu Thottayi has a 2018 street view, and Google has a satellite view. The original light on a mast was replaced by a skeletal tower in 1948. Located on the outskirts of Ponnani, just south of the Bharathpuzha river entrance. Site open, tower closed. . ARLHS IND-108; Admiralty F0692; NGA 27632.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-108</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q13113490</SimpleData>
