		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1986. Active; focal plane 33 m (108 ft); two white flashes every 20 s. 30 m (98 ft) round cylindrical concrete tower with lantern and double gallery, painted with red and white horizontal bands. Nikhil Sankar has a 2017 photo, Noufal AbdulKareem has a 2018 photo, Akhil Jyothish has a 2021 photo, and Google has a 2023 street view and a satellite view. This lighthouse has a design common to many modern Indian light towers. Located just off the beach south of Chavakkad. Site open, tower open daily in late afternoons. . ARLHS IND-082; Admiralty F0693; NGA 27564.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-082</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q18387166</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/Chetwai%20Lighthouse.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(2:Duration of Flash field says '20 Sec' while characteristic gives flash 0.46 s,Tower height given as 33.28M, identical to elevation above MSL)</SimpleData>
