		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1997. Active; focal plane 45 m (148 ft); white flash every 10 s. 45 m (148 ft) round masonry tower with lantern and double gallery, painted with horizontal red and white bands. The lantern was used previously at Pulicat Light. A 2022 photo is at right, Marcus Sherman has a 2008 photo, Mohanram Kemparaju has another photo, Vignesh Waran has a photo and a street view from atop the lighthouse, and Google has a satellite view. Kodikkarai is the Tamil name of Calimere Point. Located about 9 km (5.5 mi) west southwest of Calimere Point Light. Site status unknown, probably open. ARLHS IND-039; Admiralty F0902; NGA 27145.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-039</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q29957232</SimpleData>
