		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1969. Active; focal plane 89 m (292 ft); white flash every 15 s. 37 m (121 ft) cast iron tower with lantern and gallery painted with red and white horizontal bands. This is a staffed station with several buildings. A 2018 drone view is at right, Soma Shekar has a 2017 photo and a view from the sea, Suhit Das has a 2024 closeup, and Google has a satellite view. This lighthouse marks the northern end of the Andaman Islands. It appears to be another cast iron tower similar to the Indira Point and North Point Lights, built three years later. Located at the highest point of the island. Site status unknown. ARLHS AND-001; Admiralty F1201; NGA 26552.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">AND-001</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/KALPENI%20LIGHTHOUSE.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:Intensity printed '2.56.989 candelas' (read as 2,56,989),ALOL F 1201, RACON Sr. No 6295 and NAIS MMSI 4198001 are identical to East Island ledger values - possibly copied,RACON lists only a serial number with make/model/code blank)</SimpleData>
