		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-kochi/suhelipar-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1975. Active; focal plane 36 m (118 ft); two white flashes every 20 s. 33 m (108 ft) round cast iron tower with lantern and gallery. Lighthouse painted with horizontal red and white bands. A view from atop the lighthouse is available and Google has a satellite view of the tower. Cheriyakara is an islet at the southern end of the Suhelipar atoll; there are no permanent inhabitants but a fishing camp is occupied seasonally. This is at the southwestern corner of the Laccadives; the lighthouse marks the western entrance to the Nine Degree Channel separating Minicoy from the Laccadives. Site status unknown. ARLHS LAK-010; Admiralty F0756; NGA 27604.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">LAK-010</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/SUHELIPAR%20LIGHTHOUSE.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(4:Position printed with seconds marks after decimal values (10° 02.30&quot;, 72° 17.00&quot;); converted as decimal minutes,RACON listed (Wealth marine WM-RB-II, code O) but removed as defective on 24.01.2014,Effective beam intensity left blank,Only year of commissioning given (1975))</SimpleData>
