		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-kochi/manakkodam-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1979. Active; focal plane 34 m (112 ft); two white flashes every 10 s. 34 m (112 ft) square cylindrical concrete tower, lower half skeletal and upper half enclosed, with lantern and gallery. Lighthouse painted white; lantern roof painted red. Joseph Baiju has a view from the beach, John Alex has a good photo, Antony Simal has a 2018 photo, a 2021 photo is available, Hrishi Olickel has a distant street view from the beach, and Google has a street view and a satellite view. The lighthouse originally had red bands, but fishermen complained it could be confused with the Cochin Light, so the color patterns of the Alleppey Light and this tower were exchanged in 2000. The lighthouse marks the entra</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-099</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q18127759</SimpleData>
