		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1902 (station established 1845). Active; focal plane 29 m (95 ft); three white flashes every 9 s. 20 m (66 ft) round masonry tower, painted with horizontal black and white bands. Rishi Rajput's 2023 photo is at right, Selvamanee Rajendran has a closeup, a distant photo is available, Srinivasan KB has a 2021 photo, K.S. Chandra has a photo taken from the Pamban Channel Bridge, and Google has a satellite view of the station. The original lighthouse, listed as &quot;Palk Bay&quot; on Findlay's 1879 list, was a round 17 m (56 ft) stone tower. Pamban Island is on the Indian section of the limestone ridge known as Rama's Bridge or Adam's Bridge. The &quot;bridge&quot; was dry land as recently as 6000 years ago, but t</SimpleData>
