		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-kochi/valiazheekal-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">2021. Active; focal plane 44 m (145 ft); three white flashes every 20 s. 41 m (135) pentagonal concrete tower with lantern and gallery, painted with blue and white horizontal bands. Jyothir Rose has a photo and the view from the beach seen at right, a 2022 photo is available, Muhammed Noufal has a more distant street view, and Google has a satellite view. This is India's first pentagonal lighthouse and one of the few with an elevator. Inaugurated in October 2021, the light stands behind a popular beach and marks the entrance to a fishing harbor and intracoastal waterway. Site open, tower open daily except Mondays. . Admiralty F0709.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q135472811</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Valiyazheekkal%20Lighthouse.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:Divergence and Duration of Flash rows contain power-supply text ('Local Mains 440 V, 3 phase, 50 Hz AC supply', 'Back-up Solar Inverter supply...') instead of optic values,Effective beam intensity printed as '2,00000 cds' (irregular digit grouping); read as 200000,'No. of LED Panels 6' - panels are LED panels of a revolving beacon)</SimpleData>
