		<SimpleData name="ledger_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-12/Master%20Ledger%20Cochin%2016.pdf</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-kochi/anjengo-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1987. Active; focal plane 38 m (125 ft); two white flashes every 20 s. 36 m (118 ft) round concrete tower, painted with black and white horizontal bands. Nithin Murali's 2021 photo is at right, Akshay Raj P. has a 2023 photo, Wikimedia has a photo, a 2009 distant view is available, and Google has a street view and a satellite view. Anjengo was the site of a British East India Company fort dating to 1695. Located just outside the walls of the fort in Anchuthengu (formerly Anjengo) and about 40 km (25 mi) northwest of Thiruvananthapuram. Site open, tower open in late afternoon daily. . ARLHS IND-073; Admiralty F0715; NGA 27502.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-073</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/ANJENGO%20LIGHTHOUSE.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:No. of lens given as '06Nos (2Nos fixed and others blocked)',Divergence printed as '2.40º'; unclear whether 2.40 decimal degrees or 2°40',RACON Sr. No 6295 listed but all RACON details NA)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_since">{ }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="tenders">(1:1416)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo_credit">DGLL</SimpleData>
	</SchemaData></ExtendedData>
