		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-kochi/vizhinjam-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1972. Active; focal plane 57 m (187 ft); white flash every 15 s. 36 m (118 ft) round stone tower with lantern and gallery, painted with red and white horizontal bands; lantern dome painted red. Justin Prasad's 2022 photo is above right, Trabas has a 2018 photo, Seema Krishnakumar has a photo, Deep Goswami has a closeup, a 2009 photo and a street view from a nearby beach are available, and Google has a satellite view and a closeup street view. Foundations of a 9th century fort were discovered near the lighthouse in late 2005. Lighthouse Beach, stretching to the north toward Kovalam, is a popular tourist attraction, and as a result this lighthouse is one of the most visited lighthouses of sout</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-121</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q18395643</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Vizhinjam%20Light%20House.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(4:Printed longitude 93° 58.9' E is inconsistent with Vizhinjam, Kerala (about 77° E); transcribed as printed,Sequence FL 0.55 + ec 14.5 sums to 15.05 s, not the stated 15 s,RACON make given as Tideland Sea Beacon-2 but model as WM-RB-II,Effective beam intensity 68,38,000 cd is unusually high)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ &quot;racon&quot;: 2007 }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_since">{ &quot;racon&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2007, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;ledger&quot; }, &quot;ais&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2012, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;network&quot; } }</SimpleData>
