		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-chennai/manapad-point-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1888. Active; focal plane 45 m (148 ft); two white flashes every 10 s. Approx. 18 m (59 ft) round masonry tower painted with red and white spiral bands; lantern dome painted red. Keeper's house and several other light station buildings. Joseph Cascarino's 2022 photo is at right, Leo Fernando has a nice 2008 photo, and Google has a satellite view of the station. This well-known lighthouse adjacent to a Catholic church founded in 1581 by Portuguese missionaries. Located on Manapad Point, a prominent cape about 20 km (12.5 mi) south of Tiruchchendur. Site open, tower status unknown. . ARLHS IND-044; Admiralty F0730; NGA 27200.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-044</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q141341669</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/dg23.png</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(2:Range lists 'Luminous : 26 NM' and 'Luminous : 18 NM'; the second label is probably meant to be geographical but is printed as luminous,Latitude printed as 8°22'.3&quot; (mixed notation); converted as 8°22.3')</SimpleData>
