		<SimpleData name="ledger_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-12/Master%20Ledger%20Cochin%2032.pdf</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-kochi/minicoy-south-lighthouse-dgps-station</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1885. Active; focal plane 47 m (154 ft); white flash every 15 s. 48 m (157 ft) round brick tower with lantern and gallery. Lighthouse painted white; lantern roof is red. The lighthouse is staffed. A 2020 photo appears above, Shijo Jose has a 2017 photo, Vijay Kumar has a photo, another photo shows visitors on the gallery, Lighthouse Digest has a February 2001 feature on the lighthouse by I.C.R. Prasad, Forand has a historic postcard view, and Google has a satellite view. The island has great strategic importance because the sea route from Suez to Singapore passes through the Eight Degree Channel just south of Minicoy. To protect this lifeline of the Empire the British shipped bricks from Eng</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">LAK-009</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q22696416</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/MINICOY%20SOUTH%20LIGHTHOUSE%20%26%20DGPS%20STATION.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:Effective beam intensity printed as '3,32,15,773 cds' (33.2 million cd),Tower height '48m (up to lantern top)' highlighted in red/underlined on the page,RACON Sr. No 6295 is the same serial printed in other ledgers (e.g. Anjengo))</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ &quot;racon&quot;: 2010, &quot;ais&quot;: 2018 }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_since">{ &quot;racon&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2010, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;ledger&quot; }, &quot;ais&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2018, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;ledger&quot; }, &quot;dgps&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2003, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;network&quot; } }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="tenders">(5:2577,1831,1761,1358,700)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo_credit">DGLL</SimpleData>
	</SchemaData></ExtendedData>
