		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1883 (British; station established 1875). Active; focal plane 43 m (141 ft); white flash every 5 s. 22 m (72 ft) round masonry tower with lantern and gallery, painted with black and white horizontal bands; lantern dome painted red. A rotating 2nd order Fresnel lens is in use. Mohanraj Kolathapilly has a good closeup, Wikimedia has a 2007 photo, Raja Gopal Sunkara has a 2018 photo, Chris Jehin has an aerial view, and Google has a satellite view. A surviving British lighthouse, Muttom Light can be seen from a popular beach. Early mast and post lights here were followed by a 22 m (72 ft) granite tower in 1875. In 2013 this was also one of the 15 lighthouses identified for tourist development by</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-103</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="wikidata">Q141431205</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/dg26.jpg</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(3:Duration of Flash given as '5 second' (equal to the period),Engine 1 and Engine 2 headed '(NIL)' but Eicher 20KVA engine details listed,NAVTEX: Danphone 1KW Futronic transmitter, 518/490 kHz, Transmitter ID 'L', installed March 2015)</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ &quot;ais&quot;: 2015 }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_since">{ &quot;navtex&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2015, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;network&quot; }, &quot;racon&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2004, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;network&quot; } }</SimpleData>
