		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1909 (British; station established 1821). Active; focal plane 26 m (85 ft); white flash every 3 s. 23 m (79 ft) round cast iron tower, painted with horizontal red and white bands. The base of the lighthouse is surrounded by a square pyramidal observation platform of recent construction. A 2019 photo by Sandip Kumar Jana is at right, Nishant Kumar has a 2021 photo, Dipak Das has a 2017 photo, Santanu Sen has a 2023 photo, Partho Sarothi Mitra has a 2021 drone view, Huelse has a historic postcard view, and Google has a satellite view. The second lighthouse (1852) was also a cast iron tower. Ownership was transferred to DGLL from the Kolkata Port Trust in 2011. The present lighthouse has a very</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">IND-060</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="transcribed">1</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="ledger_issues">(4:8 panels at 7 RPM gives a flash about every 1.07 s, not every 3 s as stated,Divergence printed as '4.35 (Horiz.) &amp; 2.10 (Vert.)' without degree sign or unit,Elevation: ground 2 m, 'Elevation of tower' 26 m (used as light elevation),No commissioning date given (taken over from Kolkata Port Trust in 2011))</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_years">{ &quot;ais&quot;: 2012, &quot;dgps&quot;: 2017 }</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="equip_since">{ &quot;ais&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2012, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;ledger&quot; }, &quot;dgps&quot;: { &quot;year&quot;: 2017, &quot;src&quot;: &quot;ledger&quot; } }</SimpleData>
