		<SimpleData name="page_url">https://www.dgll.nic.in/DGLL-light-house-location/about-portblair/narcondum-lighthouse</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1983. Active; focal plane 61 m (200 ft); three white flashes every 20 s. 14 m (46 ft) square steel skeletal tower with gallery and an enclosed equipment shelter in the base. Lighthouse painted white. Trees hide the tower in Google's satellite view. Narcondam Island is an isolated volcanic peak rising abruptly from the Andaman Sea; it is uninhabited except for an Indian police contingent posted there to maintain sovereignty. Myanmar (Burma) gave up its claim to the island in a 1986 treaty. The island is a wildlife sanctuary recognized as a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Located about 120 km (75 mi) east of East Island, Narcondam is the easternmost point of Indian territory. The lighthouse is loc</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="photo">https://www.dgll.nic.in/sites/default/files/2022-11/2.png</SimpleData>
