		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1994. Active; focal plane 14 m (46 ft); two white flashes every 20 s. 12 m (39 ft) square skeletal tower with gallery and an enclosed equipment shelter in the base, painted with red and white horizontal bands. Bing has a distant satellite view. Wilson Island is an island in the central part of Ritchie's Archipelago. The light guides vessels in the narrowest section of the Diligent Strait. Located at the northwestern point of the island. Accessible only by boat. Site status unknown. Admiralty F1202.68; NGA 26518.</SimpleData>
