		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1986. Active; focal plane 51 m (167 ft); white flash every 10 s. 46 m (151 ft) cylindrical concrete tower with double gallery, painted with black and white horizontal bands. Lantern removed. A 2023 photo by Monimohan Das is at the top of this page, a 2011 photo is available, Sunny Chaurasiya has a closeup 2017 photo, there is a February 2007 closeup, Patel Dhirubhai Chhaganbhai has a 2021 photo, a photo of the view from the lighthouse is available, and Google has a satellite view. This design is common among modern lighthouses on the Indian mainland but this is the only lighthouse of this type in the Andaman and Nicobar Islands. Located at the southern tip of Little Andaman Island, marking t</SimpleData>
