		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1991. Active; focal plane 20 m (66 ft); four white flashes every 20 s. 12 m (39 ft) square steel skeletal tower with gallery and an enclosed equipment shelter in the base. Lighthouse painted white. The light is not seen in the forest in Google's satellite view. Battimalv is a small, uninhabited island about 30 km (19 mi) south of Car Nicobar. Located on the northern tip of the island. Accessible only by boat. Site open, tower closed. Admiralty F1222.4; NGA 26452.</SimpleData>
