		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1998. Active; focal plane 114 m (374 ft); white flash every 10 s. 24 m (79 ft) square steel skeletal tower with gallery and an enclosed equipment shelter in the base. Lighthouse painted with black and white horizontal bands. Google has an indistinct satellite view. 15 km (9 mi) long but only about 1 km (0.6 mi) wide, Tillanchang is a long, narrow island at the northeastern corner of the Nancowry group. It is uninhabited except for the staff of a small police station. Located on the highest point of the island. Accessible only by boat. Site open, tower closed. ARLHS AND-016; Admiralty F1222.8; NGA 26451.2.</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="arlhs">AND-016</SimpleData>
