		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1993. Active; focal plane 22 m (72 ft); two white flashes every 15 s. 12 m (39 ft) square masonry tower painted with black and white horizontal bands. A DGLL photo is at right and Google has a satellite view. The light was reported heavily damaged by the tsunami and out of service; it was rebuilt at a higher elevation. Located on the southern tip of Nancowry Island, which is about 10 km (6 mi) east of Katchall Island. Accessible by boat; land access to this site is difficult. ARLHS AND-020; Admiralty F1222.65; NGA 26450.</SimpleData>
