		<SimpleData name="rowlett">1998. Active; focal plane 62 m (203 ft); three white flashes every 20 s. 12 m (39 ft) square steel skeletal tower with gallery and an enclosed equipment shelter in the base. Lighthouse painted black with one white horizontal band. Google has an indistinct satellite view and the light is barely visible in T. Shanmukh Rao's aerial view of the island. Kabra Island is a small, heavily vegetated island about 8 km (5 mi) north of the northern tip of Great Nicobar Island. Located on the highest point of the island. Accessible only by boat. Site open, tower closed. ARLHS AND-002; Admiralty F1224.1; NGA 26437.</SimpleData>
